# Streamed replies send an SSE comment line, ": keepalive", after TENSORFOLD_SSE_KEEPALIVE_S seconds (default 15; 0:
# off) with nothing else written, on every streaming route (issue #106). A request that waits for a lane or fills a
# long prompt sends nothing after its first event, and a proxy in front cuts an idle stream (Cloudflare: after about
# two minutes). Comment lines are part of the SSE format and clients skip them; the events are the same bytes.
# cuda/http.py: _Keepalive holds the stream's writes under one lock and runs the comments from a thread only while
# App.run runs, so leaving it ends the thread before the reply's last event, its error event or a cancellation.
# server/responses.py: Wire passes the chat stream's comment lines through to the client's socket, so the Messages
# (server/anthropic.py) and Responses streams, which translate the chat stream, carry them too.
# Non-streamed replies are unchanged. A bad value stops the server at import. CPU test: tools/test_sse_keepalive.py.
diff --git tensorfold/cuda/http.py tensorfold/cuda/http.py
index 5b48deb..7360924 100644
